{"id": "20513167", "revid": "47977811", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20513167", "title": "Play God (album)", "text": "Play God is an album by the American band Reverend, released in 1991. It was Reverend's second (and last) full-length release. \"Play God\" marked the departure of bassist Dennis O'Hara and drummer Rick Basha, who were replaced by Angelo Espino and Jason Ian, respectively. The album includes a cover of Creedence Clearwater Revival's \"Fortunate Son\".\nCritical reception.\nThe \"Chicago Tribune\" wrote that Wayne \"screeches like a metal queen rather than the growly thrasher he wishes he were.\"\nAllMusic wrote that, \"under Rosen, Reverend sounded cleaner and more polished, but the heaviness and aggression remained.\"\nPersonnel.\nAdditional members"}
