{"id": "20514032", "revid": "1279536941", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20514032", "title": "\u00cele de T\u00e9r\u00e9nez", "text": "\u00cele de T\u00e9r\u00e9nez () is a French islet inside the last bend of the river Aulne, on the territory of the commune of Rosno\u00ebn. Its highest point is 18m.\nCovered in woods, it is accessible by dry land at low tide and faces the Land\u00e9vennec ship graveyard and Land\u00e9vennec Abbey. The corniche de T\u00e9r\u00e9nez, running along the right bank of the Aulne for 4 kilometres, leads to the pont de T\u00e9r\u00e9nez, located 2.5\u00a0km further upstream. The island has several locations where recreational boaters may anchor their vessels."}
